      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing Secret Manager**\n\nI've decided to use Google Secret Manager and the Google Cloud Client Library for Python to build this tool. I'm focusing on crafting the `rotate_secret_version.py` file to handle secret version reading. This choice offers a robust foundation for secure secret handling.\n\n\n**Defining Python Code**\n\nI'm now writing the `rotate_secret_version.py` file. I'm focusing on incorporating the Google Cloud Client Library to read secret versions from Google Secret Manager. I've included placeholder values for project, secret, and version IDs to start the implementation and ensure the provider (`google.cloud.secretmanager`) is clearly referenced in the code.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789820837746,
          "start": 1789820835447
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
